Here's another Crawl-ism that I've transported - albeit in a radically
changed form - to NetHack: eating the corpse of a thick-skinned monster
requires a blade to be wielded first.

* There is a sharpness check performed on the blade first - and weapons
which are still keen enough to cut small monsters may be too blunt for
big monsters.
* Using a corrodeable blade on an acidic corpse corrodes the blade.
After observing this, the player may abort the eating if they wish.
* If you are polymorphed into a form with a biting attack that is
larger than the corpse, you may then use your teeth as usual (for which
no particular message is given.)

